#     cannot complete a TLS handshake through this session's egress proxy
#     AT ALL, even to https://example.com. net::ERR_CONNECTION_RESET,
#     SSL error code 1 (net/socket/socket_bio_adapter.cc), 100% reproducible.
#   - Ruled out via --log-net-log + --enable-logging=stderr and targeted
#     flag combinations: --ignore-certificate-errors, --disable-http2,
#     --disable-quic, --no-sandbox, --disable-features=EncryptedClientHello,
#     PostQuantumKyber, PermuteTLSExtensions, UseDnsHttpsSvcbAlpn (singly
#     and combined) -- none change the outcome.
#   - curl, openssl s_client (TLS1.2 and TLS1.3), and Node's `ws` package
#     with an explicit https-proxy-agent ALL succeed through the IDENTICAL
#     proxy against the IDENTICAL hosts (example.com, preview-aws.
#     vitanaland.com, preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com) -- isolating the
#     failure to Chromium's own TLS stack specifically, not the proxy, not
