# Forensic evidence gathering -- read-only queries against oasis_events for
# the exact live staging window the user reported (08:05-08:09 UTC,
# 2026-08-25), correlated with source reading:
supabase execute_sql --project inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb \
  "SELECT created_at, topic, metadata->>'session_id', metadata->>'stage', ...
   FROM oasis_events WHERE created_at BETWEEN '2026-08-25 08:05:00+00' AND '2026-08-25 08:09:00+00' ...
   ORDER BY created_at ASC;"
#   -> Found: guided-topic session 912f74a8 won the wake-brief ranker
#      correctly (guided_topic_audio_bridge_sent fired), then hit
#      nova_validation TWICE at turn_count=0 (no audio ever played), was
#      superseded by a BRAND NEW session 06fb8ada (client-side
#      _attemptReconnect giving up and calling _sessionStart fresh, not a
#      same-session server retry). Session 06fb8ada never emitted
#      guided_topic_audio_bridge_sent at all and instead delivered
#      wake_opener=newday_overview -- the VTID-03724 symptom, reproduced
#      via a DIFFERENT mechanism than the one VTID-03724 fixed.

# Read orb-widget.js's _attemptReconnect() (line ~4063) -- confirmed it
# unconditionally calls _setStatus(_caption('reconnecting')) before every
# retry, regardless of _s.greetingComplete, unlike _announceDisconnect()
# (per-reason labels) and the already-fixed VTID-03685 WS-error-frame
# suppression ("hasHeardNothingYet" pattern). This call site was never
# covered by that fix.

# Read orb-live.ts's sendGreetingPromptToLiveAPI() _openDecision build
# (line ~10031 pre-fix) and opening-contract.ts's decideOpening() --
# confirmed decideOpening() returns mode:'silent' whenever isReconnect is
# true (regardless of wakeSelectedLine) OR whenever wakeCadenceSkip is true
# (<~120s since session.lastSessionInfo, BOOTSTRAP-NOVA-GREETING-CADENCE).
# tryGuidedTopicRung (compute-greeting-decision.ts) composes its ENTIRE
# spoken line from ctx.openDecision.line and only fires when
# ctx.openDecision.mode==='speak' -- so it can be silenced by a completely
# unrelated cadence heuristic even while ctx.guidedTopicNarrationContent is
# present. session 06fb8ada is a BRAND NEW session object (own
# _reconnectCount starts at 0, so isReconnect itself reads false there
# regardless of the existing _freshOpenAfterZeroTurnRecovery flag, which is
# scoped to SAME-session server-internal retries only) -- but
# wakeCadenceSkip still fires, because the failed prior session (912f74a8)
# ended only ~1-3s earlier.

# Implementation:
#  1. orb-widget.js: _attemptReconnect()'s status caption gated on
#     _s.greetingComplete ('connecting' when nothing heard yet,
#     'reconnecting' once real audio has played).
#  2. orb-live.ts: new _hasPendingGuidedTopicAtOpen
#     (!!session.guidedTopicNarrationContent && session.turn_count===0)
#     suppresses BOTH isReconnect and wakeCadenceSkip in the
#     sendGreetingPromptToLiveAPI() _openDecision build. Gated on THIS
#     session's own turn_count (not the prior session's) so a genuine
#     mid-lesson reconnect (turn_count>0) is completely unaffected --
#     silent_reconnect (compute-greeting-decision.ts rung 7, which reads
#     openDecision.source) still wins, per VTID-03724's AC-5.

